From d154f640a7291947a2f1aff0816b43dbda0f033b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk <patryk@Patryks-MacBook.local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:13:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Cockpit LED: sparse, fresh flavour and shorter, clearer
 messages

- Shorten the sign's idle and hint copy and drop FAST: the skip hint is SKIP
  (also CLEAR/FLIP/CANCEL/BLOOM, and GROW/BLOOM as the resting instructions).
- Add web/src/player/led-flavour.ts: short reaction pools per moment kind, drawn
  from a shuffled bag so a line cannot repeat until its pool is exhausted. A
  reproducible gate shows flavour on ~14% of eligible moments and a kind never
  speaks twice in a row; pools reset each match.
- display-readout: emit the plain fact first (CUT-N, +N, YOU WIN...), with an
  optional flavour pool, an optional cut/bloom accent and a wait pulse.
- display-machine: show the fact for its full duration, then allow a flavour tail
  only; pass flash/pulse through the frame.
- led-cells: ledToken() shortens known captions/banners for the physical window
  only, leaving the live region's full sentence intact; adds short static
  mappings (FUTASAKU, CANCEL, CUT-N).
- smart-cockpit: one-shot cut/bloom flash and a subtle WAIT/OPP pulse on the
  window, both skipped under reduce-motion.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
